{
 "duration": 25.183,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Wet leaves hide slick rock.",
   "start": 0.4,
   "end": 1.905
  },
  {
   "text": "One slip, and Ana caught herself on her hands.",
   "start": 2.355,
   "end": 4.743
  },
  {
   "text": "Gravel in the scrape, three miles still to go.",
   "start": 5.193,
   "end": 7.642
  },
  {
   "text": "Wiping it on her pants would only push the dirt in.",
   "start": 8.092,
   "end": 10.756
  },
  {
   "text": "So she stopped.",
   "start": 11.206,
   "end": 12.037
  },
  {
   "text": "She rinsed the scrape with clean water from her bottle until the grit was gone,",
   "start": 12.487,
   "end": 16.5
  },
  {
   "text": "patted it dry, and covered it with a bandage from the kit that lives in her daypack.",
   "start": 16.95,
   "end": 21.372
  },
  {
   "text": "Then she walked out.",
   "start": 21.822,
   "end": 22.861
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this for your next fall hike.",
   "start": 23.311,
   "end": 24.983
  }
 ],
